## Original English prose used by analysis tests (about 1,100 letters).

const TEXT: String = "The marsh was quiet when the brothers came down to the water, and the reeds leaned over them like old men listening at a door. Kett had walked these paths for thirty years and he still counted every step, because the ground here changed its mind with every tide. He told the boy that a letter is only a road that someone else has built, and that the trick is to walk it slowly and look for the places where the builder was lazy. The boy asked how anyone could see laziness in a line of strange marks. Kett laughed and said that people are the same in every alphabet. They repeat themselves. They begin their letters in the same way and they end them in the same way, and in between they complain about the weather, the price of salt, and the servants who steal candles. Find the thing a man cannot stop himself from saying, and you have found the door into everything else he wrote. The boy did not believe him that night. By the end of the winter he believed nothing else, and he had learned to read the mail of monsters by the light of a single candle while the wind moved over the water and the village slept."
